Lab 11: Namespace Management and Resource Quota Enforcement
1. Create the namespace
bash
kubectl create namespace ivolve
kubectl get namespaces
2. Create the ResourceQuota (max 3 pods)

Imperative:
bash
kubectl create quota ivolvequota --hard=pods=3 -n ivolve -o yaml > quota.yml

quota.yml:
yaml
apiVersion: v1
kind: ResourceQuota
metadata:
  name: ivolvequota
  namespace: ivolve
spec:
  hard:
    pods: "3"

3. Verify the quota
bash
kubectl get resourcequota -n ivolve
kubectl describe resourcequota ivolvequota -n ivolve
# Resource  Used  Hard
# pods      0     3
4. Confirm Kubernetes blocks extra pods

Create 3 pods, then a 4th:

bash
kubectl run pod1 --image=nginx -n ivolve
kubectl run pod2 --image=nginx -n ivolve
kubectl run pod3 --image=nginx -n ivolve

kubectl run pod4 --image=nginx -n ivolve
# Error from server (Forbidden): pods "pod4" is forbidden:
# exceeded quota: ivolvequota, requested: pods=1, used: pods=3, limited: pods=3

Check usage again:

bash
kubectl describe resourcequota ivolvequota -n ivolve    # pods 3/3
kubectl get pods -n ivolve
